{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>You</b> — Rabbi Moses said: every creature that dives in the sea and whose body is large is called Leviathan, and the sign is that he said \"heads\" and not \"head.\" In my opinion: Leviathan is a large fish and the word \"every\" is missing, as in \"the heads of every Leviathan.\" And so HaShem gave it as food to the people of the desert-dwellers, who dwell in the desert opposite the sea, and it is known that there are places where they eat it from time to time at a known season. And Rabbi Moses said: \"to a people of desert-dwellers\" is like \"to your servant Jacob.\" And the meaning of \"desert-dwellers\" — the people of the ships."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 74, :notes {0 "I read לציים as a plural of לץ (coastal/desert dweller); Ibn Ezra's own paraphrase glosses it as people of the ships. The root לצה appears to be his reading; whether it relates to צי (ship) or צייה (dry land) is left unresolved in the text."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:31.305555303Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}